/*  Regions — `Pull a rabbit` and the rule that keeps one sound: `CheckPullRabbit`,
    `CheckRegionStore`, `ValueDepthOf` and `ContainerDepthOf` in
    `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.Rabbit.cs`.

    ★ A region is a depth. Pulling a rabbit goes one deeper, a name remembers the depth it was made
    at, and a value may not be stored anywhere that outlives it — somewhere shallower.

    ★ What a CALL or a member read gives back is as deep as its signature says — see
    `region-depths.cufe`, which works that out once each function's body has been checked.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// What a series, a map, a set, a chase, an object — anything held by reference — is; a value-typed one copies.
    Bind fact to is-reference-type, given (the node shape):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        Return kind is "SeriesType" or kind is "MapType" or kind is "SetType" or kind is "ChaseType" or kind is "ObjectType" or kind is "MatrixType"
            or kind is "ChannelType" or kind is "AddressType".
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-rabbit-type, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is not "ObjectType", return false.
        Return (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)) in lowercase) is "rabbit".
    Done.

    /// How deep a captured parameter is taken to be: deeper than anything, so it is stored nowhere.
    Bind number to captured-parameter-depth:
        Return 2147483647.
    Done.

    /// The depth of the container being written into — its name's, or where the write stands.
    Bind number to container-depth unto checker, given (the node target):
        If target's kind is "VariableReference":
            Define found as cast one's look-up on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1))).
            If found is not void, return found's depth.
        Done.
        Return one's rabbit-depth.
    Done.

    /// `IsRegionBearing`: whether a type's compiled form holds an arena pointer anywhere in its
    /// shape — text and every collection do, a record or a voidable when something inside does, an
    /// open union always.
    Bind fact to is-region-bearing unto checker, given (the node shape):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        If kind is "TextType" or kind is "SeriesType" or kind is "MapType" or kind is "SetType" or kind is "ChaseType" or kind is "MatrixType" or kind is "ChannelType"
                or kind is "FunctionType" or kind is "StashType" or kind is "ObjectType":
            Return true.
        Done.
        If kind is "RecordType":
            For each part in (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's is-region-bearing on (part), return true.
            Done.
            For each pair in (cast field-of on (shape, 2))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's is-region-bearing on (item 2 of pair's children), return true.
            Done.
            Return false.
        Done.
        If kind is "VoidableType" or kind is "FailureType", return cast one's is-region-bearing on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
        If kind is "UnionType":
            If cast is-open-union on (shape), return true.
            For each member in (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's is-region-bearing on (member), return true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// `EscapeDepthFor`: where a stored value must be copied to — the destination's depth — when it
    /// would outlive its own region there, or -1. A value holding no region memory counts as made
    /// where the store stands, which is what decides whether the destination's own growth moves.
    Bind number to escape-depth-for unto checker, given (the node value, the node value-type, the number target-depth):
        If cast one's escaping-from on (value, value-type) is greater than target-depth, return target-depth.
        Return -1.
    Done.

    /// How deep the region a stored value would be leaving is.
    Bind number to escaping-from unto checker, given (the node value, the node value-type):
        Define value-depth as one's rabbit-depth.
        If value-type's kind is "FunctionType", return cast one's lives-at on (value).
        If cast one's is-region-bearing on (value-type):
            Define kind as value's kind.
            If kind is "VariableReference":
                Define found as cast one's look-up on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (value, 1))).
                If found is not void, the value-depth becomes found's depth.
            Done.
            If kind is "CastExpression":
                Define cached as the entry for cast node-place on (value, 3) in one's call-depths.
                If cached is not void, the value-depth becomes cached.
            Done.
            If kind is "PossessiveAccess" or kind is "RecordNamedAccess":
                Define cached-member as the entry for cast node-place on (value, 3) in one's member-depths.
                If cached-member is not void, the value-depth becomes cached-member.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return value-depth.
    Done.

    /// Writes C#'s `EscapeToDepth` (or `KeyEscapeToDepth`, by `mark`) onto a store — the depth a
    /// compiler copies the value out to. Never refuses anything. A depth of 0 is written as nothing,
    /// as C#'s tree prints it.
    Bind void to note-escape unto checker, given (the node statement, the text mark, the node value,
            the node value-type, the number target-depth):
        Define depth as cast one's escape-depth-for on (value, value-type, target-depth).
        If depth is greater than 0, cast note on (statement, mark, cast numeral on (depth)).
        Otherwise, cast note on (statement, mark, cast nothing).
    Done.

    // ── Where a shared constant lives ────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Where a `Define` stands, as the key its constant is known by.
    Bind text to define-place, given (the node statement):
        Return "{(cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s word}:{(cast field-of on (statement, 6))'s word}".
    Done.

    /// Where the value of a `permanently` constant lives: "" when nothing has to place it, "Made" or
    /// "Copied" into the program's region, or "OfItsBlock" when it is its block's own. `PlaceOfConstant`
    /// in C#, where the reason is.
    Bind text or failure to place-of-constant unto checker, given (the node statement, the node shape, the fact hoisted):
        If (the entry for cast define-place on (statement) in one's shared-defines) is void, return "".
        // A constant that hides the program's own cannot take its place.
        If cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)), return "OfItsBlock".
        If one's rabbit-depth is 0 or cast is-held-in-region on (shape) is false, return "".
        Define refs as a map from text to fact.
        Define defs as a map from text to fact.
        Cast refs-and-defs on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), refs, defs).
        Define holding as 0.
        Define all-free as true.
        For each pair in refs, repeat:
            Define found as cast one's look-up on (the key of pair).
            If found is not void:
                If found's depth is greater than 0 and found's module is false and cast is-held-in-region on (found's shape):
                    If found's shape's kind is not "FunctionType" or cast one's is-program-function on (the key of pair, found) is false:
                        Increment holding by 1.
                        If cast one's is-container-free on (found's shape) is false, the all-free becomes false.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        If holding is 0, return "Made".
        If cast one's copies-out on (shape, a map from text to fact):
            If all-free or cast one's is-container-free on (shape), return "Copied".
        Done.
        If hoisted is false, return "OfItsBlock".
        // Registered for the whole program by a reading of its value that its own line does not bear
        // out: a name it uses is shadowed here.
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
            "this value lives in a shorter-lived region than its destination — it will be gone when that region ends", "",
            cast number-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)), "keep it in '{name}', which lives as long as the program",
            "Declare the container inside that region too, so both end at its 'Done.', or make the value before the region opens, so it lives as long as the container.")).
    Done.

    /// A value of this type can hold something a region owns.
    Bind fact to is-held-in-region, given (the node shape):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        If kind is "NumberType" or kind is "BitsType" or kind is "FactType" or kind is "VoidType" or kind is "BookType", return false.
        If kind is "VoidableType", return cast is-held-in-region on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
        If kind is "UnionType" and cast is-open-union on (shape) is false:
            For each member in (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast is-held-in-region on (member), return true.
            Done.
            Return false.
        Done.
        If kind is "RecordType":
            For each positional in (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast is-held-in-region on (positional), return true.
            Done.
            For each named in (cast field-of on (shape, 2))'s children, repeat:
                If cast is-held-in-region on (cast field-of on (named, 2)), return true.
            Done.
            Return false.
        Done.
        Return true.
    Done.

    /// A value of this type holds nothing two names could share and one of them change.
    Bind fact to is-container-free unto checker, given (the node shape):
        Return cast one's field-holds-container on (shape, a map from text to fact) is false.
    Done.

    /// A value of this type can be copied whole into another region.
    Bind fact to copies-out unto checker, given (the node shape, the map from text to fact seen):
        Define kind as shape's kind.
        If kind is "NumberType" or kind is "BitsType" or kind is "FactType" or kind is "VoidType" or kind is "TextType"
                or kind is "ChaseType" or kind is "MatrixType":
            Return true.
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesType" or kind is "SetType" or kind is "VoidableType", return cast one's copies-out on (cast field-of on (shape, 1), seen).
        If kind is "MapType":
            Return cast one's copies-out on (cast field-of on (shape, 1), seen) and cast one's copies-out on (cast field-of on (shape, 2), seen).
        Done.
        If kind is "UnionType" and cast is-open-union on (shape) is false:
            For each member in (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's copies-out on (member, seen) is false, return false.
            Done.
            Return true.
        Done.
        If kind is "RecordType":
            For each positional in (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's copies-out on (positional, seen) is false, return false.
            Done.
            For each named in (cast field-of on (shape, 2))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's copies-out on (cast field-of on (named, 2), seen) is false, return false.
            Done.
            Return true.
        Done.
        If kind is "ObjectType":
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
            If (the entry for name in seen) is not void, return true.
            In seen, the entry for name becomes true.
            Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (name).
            If definition is void, return false.
            For each positional in (cast field-of on (definition, 2))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's copies-out on (positional, seen) is false, return false.
            Done.
            For each named in (cast field-of on (definition, 3))'s children, repeat:
                If cast one's copies-out on (cast field-of on (named, 2), seen) is false, return false.
            Done.
            Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
            If embedded is not "", return cast one's copies-out on (cast object-type-named on (embedded), seen).
            Return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// A value stored where it would outlive its region is refused.
    Bind void or failure to check-region-store unto checker, given (the node value, the node value-type,
            the number target-depth, the number at-row, the text action):
        If cast is-reference-type on (value-type) is false, return.
        Define value-depth as cast one's depth-of-value on (value, value-type).
        If value-depth is greater than target-depth, return a failure (cast shorter-lived on (at-row, action)).
    Done.

    Bind text to shorter-lived, given (the number at-row, the text action):
        Return cast refusal-of on (
            "this value lives in a shorter-lived region than its destination — it will be gone when that region ends", "",
            at-row, action,
            "Declare the container inside that region too, so both end at its 'Done.', or make the value before the region opens, so it lives as long as the container.").
    Done.

    /// `Pull a rabbit [as <name>].` — one region deeper for the length of the block.
    Bind void or failure to check-pull-rabbit unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast number-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        // How its tasks compose: "automatic", "sequential", "parallel", or "" when nothing was said.
        Define mode as "".
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)) is false, the mode becomes cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)).
        Insert mode into one's rabbit-modes.
        Insert the number of one's scopes + 1 into one's rabbit-scopes.
        Increment one's rabbit-depth by 1.
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        Define named as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        If cast is-nothing on (named) is false:
            Define name as cast unquoted on (named).
            Cast one's bind-name on (name, a new binding {
                the shape cast object-type-named on ("rabbit"),
                the established-by cast placed-reference on (name, at-row, cast number-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 4))),
                the line at-row, the permanent false, the module false, the depth one's rabbit-depth, the parameter false, the judged false }).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's exit-scope.
        Decrement one's rabbit-depth by 1.
        Remove item (the number of one's rabbit-modes) from one's rabbit-modes.
        Remove item (the number of one's rabbit-scopes) from one's rabbit-scopes.
    Done.
Done.
